# Git must not transform any file in this repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# The trusted export is verified by BYTES. `ExportDataSource.descriptor()` reads all 253
# evidence files, hashes them, and compares the result against `EXPORT_BASELINE_SHA` -- the
# digest every Phase 1-8 guarantee was established against. A source whose digest does not match
# is marked FAILED, and `bind_source` then refuses to let it serve the engine. That is the
# integrity mechanism doing its job.
#
# Git's line-ending conversion breaks it. With `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Git for
# Windows) git stores CRLF working-copy files as LF blobs, so a Linux host -- Streamlit Community
# Cloud, a container, CI -- checks out different bytes than the machine the export was built on.
# All 253 evidence files were altered this way, the digest changed, and the application refused
# to start with a QuarantineError. Correctly: the evidence really had been modified in transit.
#
# `-text` disables that conversion entirely. Git stores and restores every byte exactly as it is,
# on every platform, so the export that is verified here is the export that is served there.
#
# The rule is `*` rather than `*.csv` deliberately: the digest covers whatever the manifest
# names, and a future evidence file with a different extension must be protected without anyone
# having to remember to add it here.
* -text

# Language hints only. These affect GitHub's diff and language statistics, never file contents.
*.csv linguist-generated=true
*.zip binary
